      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rancho Santa Margarita takes its name from the historic Mexican land grant Rancho Santa Margarita y Las Flores, established in 1841.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoverorangecounty.net/city-guides/rancho-santa-margarita/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city is one of Orange County’s youngest, officially incorporated in 1992 as a master‑planned community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rancho_Santa_Margarita%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "It sits atop Plano Trabuco, a high plateau that gives the town its distinctive rolling hills and panoramic views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
